id: pm-0orupq
title: Preserve authoritative history after native SQLite transaction startup failures
description: "Native packed-consumer diagnostics identify ERR_SQLITE_ERROR disk I/O failures on Bun1.4.0 macOSarm64, including zero-winner concurrent creates. Controlled real-SQLite adapters reproduce authority loss when optional history-index PRAGMA or BEGIN startup fails. Invalidate that derived projection before authoritative append for recognized native failures, preserve existing contention and unrelated-error handling, and retain failure diagnostics for platform acceptance."
type: Task
status: closed
priority: 1
tags[3]: bug,ci,sdk
created_at: "2026-10-19T19:40:27.190Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-19T21:07:22.545Z"
closed_at: "2026-10-19T20:41:01.569Z"
completed_at: "2026-10-19T20:41:01.569Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 60
acceptance_criteria: Recognized native SQLite failures at PRAGMA and BEGIN cannot prevent an authoritative append; Invalidation precedes fallback and stale indexed data is never certified; Genuine authoritative append errors propagate exactly once and unrelated adapter failures retain their previous refusal behavior; Native contention retains its existing protocol and later index rebuild recovers complete history; Both packed public conflict guards and one-winner one-loser acceptance remain unchanged on Node and Bun; Original hosted failures are retained and revised native Mac validation is assessed independently
parent: pm-u9d0
risk: medium
confidence: medium
resolution: "Preserve runtime and typed rejection diagnostics, then handle recognized native SQLite failures during history-index PRAGMA or BEGIN startup by invalidating the optional projection before authoritative append. Preserve contention behavior, unrelated adapter refusal and exact-once authoritative error propagation; later index rebuild restores complete accelerated reads."
expected_result: "Optional SQLite transaction startup damage cannot abort authoritative history, stale indexes remain untrusted, and the packed public one-winner conflict contract stays intact on Node and Bun."
actual_result: "Native e30d553 diagnostics identify ERR_SQLITE_ERROR disk I/O on Bun1.4.0 macOSarm64 while seven other jobs pass. Controlled PRAGMA and BEGIN cases reproduce the same error class and fail before the repair; afterward all64 history/snapshot cases pass, preserving unrelated-error refusal, exact-once authoritative failures and later complete repair. Both linked commands pass65 cases including real packed Node/Bun acceptance with unchanged assertions. Broader337 cases pass exact scoped100 percent. The underlying native I/O cause is not claimed repaired; revised hosted Mac acceptance remains required before merge."
