comments[8]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-19T19:40:27.190Z","harness:codex","Duplicate check: complete 207 open / 1 active lists plus packed-conflict diagnostic search show no matching live diagnostic owner. Full closed pm-58zon0 and complete history describe shipped one-winner/lock-conflict qualification; this is a new zero-winner recurrence. Source22ed passes both native Mac shards, while a235 and6385 fail the Bun assertion. One unchanged failed-job rerun of6385 is now running; original traces remain preserved."
  "2026-10-19T19:50:11.868Z","harness:codex","Added a failure-only diagnostic containing runtime versions/platform, the requested conflict id, every settled outcome and rejected name/code/message/context. The exact one-winner/one-loser assertions, both typed guards and settlement reread remain unchanged. Current real packed Node26 and Bun acceptance passes all19 continuation cases and both conflict guards. An isolated before/after fault control forces the two runtimes to reuse one id: both old and new fixtures correctly fail, but only the new fixture identifies typed item_already_exists rejections. This proves diagnostic value, not the cause of the historical Mac failure; native evidence remains required."
  "2026-10-19T20:00:43.214Z","harness:codex","The one unchanged rerun of6385 now completes all eight Nightly jobs successfully, including both full Windows/macOS shards and Linux22/24/25. Attempt1 retains the Windows30-second settlement timeout and Mac Bun zero-winner failure. No runtime cause is inferred from the green rerun. The new failure-only diagnostic will be reviewed with the retry fix and exercised by the next native run; all assertions timeouts and retries stay unchanged."
  "2026-10-19T20:01:58.087Z","harness:codex","The linked real npm-tarball Node/Bun continuation acceptance also passes through pm test with recorded sandbox provenance. The isolated forced collision verifies that the added message distinguishes two typed duplicate rejections while preserving failure. Diagnostic implementation is complete, but the historical zero-winner root cause remains unqualified; retain this investigation open and release its claim rather than recording a fabricated runtime fix. The next source-head native run remains delivery acceptance."
  "2026-10-19T20:28:33.393Z","harness:codex","Native39316217700 at e30d553 completes seven jobs green, including quality all Linux versions and both Windows shards; Mac shard1 fails the original packed Bun conflict assertion. The new diagnostic identifies both rejected creates as ERR_SQLITE_ERROR with disk I/O error on Bun1.4.0 macOSarm64. Another retained attempt has one winner and a loser with the same SQLite error. Claim the existing investigation to trace this concrete database path without weakening assertions."
  "2026-10-19T20:33:26.345Z","harness:codex","Controlled failure injection through the existing SQLite constructor seam reproduces the same native disk-I/O error class at both PRAGMA setup and BEGIN IMMEDIATE. Both new authority-preservation controls fail before the repair, while an unrelated adapter-exception control passes unchanged. The candidate handles only recognized native SQLite startup failures, invalidates the optional projection before appending, and retains native contention handling and unrecognized-error refusal. Tests also preserve exact-once propagation of genuine authoritative append errors and verify subsequent index repair. Hosted Mac acceptance still determines whether this closes the observed native path."
  "2026-10-19T20:37:08.219Z","harness:codex","The complete existing history/index-snapshot cohort passes64 cases with the new startup-failure controls, including later repair and exact-once authoritative failure propagation. Strict lint and all four TypeScript projects pass. Initial323-case broader scope also passes every test; its scoped coverage omissions are pre-existing harness/filter and separate conflict-guard cases, now being covered through their existing suites. Real packed acceptance and revised native Mac validation remain outstanding delivery checks."
  "2026-10-19T21:07:22.545Z","harness:codex","Hosted acceptance now passes on fixing source dd097e4e1 in Nightly39321886786: all eight jobs succeed, including both complete Mac shards. Mac shard1 passes5169 cases plus three intentional skips, emits both packed Node/Bun continuation receipts and has no packed create outcome assertion. The original e30d553 SQLite failures remain retained. This validates the fallback and unchanged public guards on native Mac; it does not claim the underlying Bun engine I/O cause repaired."
